6. DOCUMENTATION OF CHANGES
---------------------------

6.1 CHANGES FILE

Every Fork or Derivative Work must include a file named "changes.md" in its
root directory.

The file must contain a clear, human-readable record of all modifications
made relative to the Original Software. Each entry must include, at minimum:

(a) a description of the change;

(b) the date on which the change was made; and

(c) the name or handle of the person or organization responsible for the
    change.

6.2 INLINE COMMENTS

Modified source-code sections must include inline comments, placed directly
adjacent to the modified code where reasonably practicable, identifying:

(a) what was changed;

(b) why the change was made, to the extent reasonably possible; and

(c) who made the change.

This requirement does not require disclosure of information that the person
making the change is legally prohibited from disclosing.

